          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_scale" value="&lt;b&gt;Who owns what&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The controller owns builds: it derives a build ID from the pod template, creates one Deployment per build, ramps new workflows onto it through the Temporal API and deletes it once drained. KEDA owns replicas: spec.replicas is absent from both WorkerDeployments, and each build's ScaledObject (rendered from order-fulfillment-scaler / checkout-abandon-scaler) sets 1–3 pods from that build's own backlog. The only replica write the controller keeps is the sunset: drained + 1 h → 0, then delete." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1060" width="1140" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_scope" value="&lt;b&gt;Out of this picture&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The order worker also runs the start-outbox dispatcher, which retries a workflow start the API could not make inline (docs/api/temporal.md § How the Saga Gets Started). Both workers and the server export telemetry: worker SDK metrics go OTLP to the collector and on to vmagent; the server's ServiceMonitors are scraped by vmagent. The KEDA board (Grafana uid keda) graphs backlog, desired vs current replicas per build." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1142" width="1140" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" value="Legend" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;verticalAlign=top;html=1;container=1;collapsible=0;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#334155;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1232" width="1140" height="88" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
